= a
{parent=2}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=a}

Apply the <chain rule> to the exponential, differentiating its exponent $-x^2$:
$$
\boxed{\frac d{dx}e^{-x^2}=-2xe^{-x^2}.}
$$

= b
{parent=2}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

The <derivative> of the <hyperbolic sine> is the <hyperbolic cosine>. Hence the <chain rule> gives
$$
\boxed{\frac d{dx}\sinh^2x=2\sinh x\cosh x=\sinh2x.}
$$

= 3
