= a
{parent=7}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=a}

This <geometric series> has first term $1$ and ratio $0.999$, which lies strictly inside the unit <interval>. Therefore
$$
\boxed{\sum_{n=0}^{\infty}(0.999)^n=\frac1{1-0.999}=1000.}
$$
The decimal is treated as the exact value $999/1000$.

= b
{parent=7}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

There are $N+1$ terms, namely $1,2,\ldots,N+1$. The <arithmetic series> formula gives
$$
\boxed{\sum_{n=0}^{N}(n+1)=\frac{(N+1)(N+2)}2,\qquad N\in\mathbb Z_{\geq0}.}
$$
Pairing the first and last terms gives pair sum $N+2$, explaining both factors.

